          "source_version": "8",
          "authority": "reference_only",
          "trust": "verified",
          "freshness": "2026-08-25T11:00:00Z",
          "relevance": 2.334,
          "lineage": "verbatim",
          "injection_risk": "untrusted_content",
          "body": "Once the test succeeds, turn on Require SSO. Members then must sign in through the identity provider, and password sign-in is disabled for them. Workspace owners keep a password as a recovery path in case the identity provider is down."
        },
        {
          "token_budget": null,
          "variants": [],
          "conflict_policy": "defers",
          "eligibility": "route-policy",
          "id": "help:sso@8#4",
          "slot": "evidence.knowledge",
          "source": "help-center:sso",
          "source_version": "8",
          "authority": "reference_only",
          "trust": "verified",
          "freshness": "2026-08-25T11:00:00Z",
          "relevance": 2.135,
          "lineage": "verbatim",
          "injection_risk": "untrusted_content",
          "body": "SCIM provisioning creates, updates and deactivates Fernway members from your identity provider. Generate a SCIM token under Single sign-on, then SCIM, and paste it with the SCIM base URL into Okta or Entra ID. Deactivating a user in the identity provider removes their seat in Fernway within minutes."
        },
        {
          "token_budget": null,
          "variants": [],
          "conflict_policy": "defers",
          "eligibility": "route-policy",
          "id": "help:sso@8#1",
          "slot": "evidence.knowledge",
          "source": "help-center:sso",
          "source_version": "8",
          "authority": "reference_only",
          "trust": "verified",
          "freshness": "2026-08-25T11:00:00Z",
          "relevance": 1.87,
          "lineage": "verbatim",
          "injection_risk": "untrusted_content",
          "body": "To set up SSO, a workspace owner opens Settings, then Security, then Single sign-on, and copies Fernway's ACS URL and entity ID into a new SAML app in the identity provider. Then paste the provider's metadata URL back into Fernway and choose Test connection."
        },
        {
          "token_budget": null,
          "variants": [],
          "conflict_policy": "defers",
          "eligibility": "route-policy",
          "id": "help:projects@4#3",
